---
description: Rules for automated GitHub PR fixing
alwaysApply: true
---
Automated GitHub fixes are restricted to ordinary documentation, source and test changes.
Never run DISM, mount images, modify host networking, provision VMs or VHDs, elevate privileges, activate Layer D, change servicing authorizations, or build an ISO.
Never edit .github/, automation/, .cursor/, postinstall/, authorization/safety code, or high-risk manifests.
Never run git, gh, curl, or arbitrary external shell commands; do not access credentials.
Never merge. Make minimal changes for the exact reviewed findings. Any unsafe request must be declined.
